1. `technical/web-platform-security.md`
   - New section 13 "Hardening run" with seven parts:
     - **13.1 What changed:** the DB guards, including migrations 20261018 and 20261019.
     - **13.2 Threat rows T75-T85.**
     - **13.3 How it works:**
       - the three four-eyes bases in order;
       - the label-author definition;
       - the 50-label truncation flag and the tenant-wide exclusion;
       - client address via CloudFront-Viewer-Address and origin-verify;
       - change-password lock;
       - MFA-promotion revocation;
       - invite parity;
       - the known-device rule;
       - canonical lower-case ids;
       - failure transparency.
     - **13.4 Status table:** each item marked closed, narrowed or unchanged, with its exact remainder. It covers SC-1, SC-2, SC-8, DD-3, DD-6, FE-S2 (packets, UPDATE only), FE-N1, SA-1..SA-6, SA-8, SA-11, FO-1, FO-10, P1-P5, F-03 and H-1..H-5.
