4. `ARCHITECTURE.no.md` — the same part in Norwegian, with identical Mermaid blocks.
5. `README.md`
   - A new section "Hardening: improvements to existing features". It covers the four-eyes basis texts, failed-analysis reasons and the claim-sheet note, bulk order and stop lines, the Charges influence section, the wording changes, and the account changes. Account changes are the change-password lockout, known-device login, MFA promotion, invite 201 and the client address. All UI strings are quoted verbatim from transparency-copy.ts.
   - An overview bullet pointing to it.
   - I also corrected step 5 and four-eyes text that the run made wrong: the old "You edited this revision" message, "the dialog does not say the budget stopped the run", and oldest-first retries of failing claims.
6. `README.no.md` — the same changes in Norwegian.
7. `docs/secrets.md` — ORIGIN_VERIFY_SECRET and CLIENT_IP_HEADER: start-up and production rules, inventory rows, the HR-8 note on public test values, and a rotation row. The secret lives in its own Secrets Manager container, `<name>/origin-verify-secret`, and is also held in the CloudFront header and the ALB rule, set out of band. No values anywhere.
